# Secret Detection

## High-Confidence Patterns (Always Flag)

| Type | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| AWS Access Key | `AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}` |
| GitHub Token | `ghp_[A-Za-z0-9]{36,}` or `github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{82}` |
| GitLab Token | `glpat-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}` |
| Slack Bot Token | `xoxb-[0-9]{10,}-[0-9]{10,}-[A-Za-z0-9]{24,}` |
| Stripe Key | `[sr]k_(live\|test)_[A-Za-z0-9]{24,}` |
| SendGrid Key | `SG\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{43}` |
| Private Key | `-----BEGIN (RSA\|EC\|OPENSSH\|PGP )?PRIVATE KEY` |
| DB Connection | `postgres://[^:]+:[^@]+@` or `mysql://[^:]+:[^@]+@` or `mongodb://[^:]+:[^@]+@` |
| Generic Secret | `(?i)(password\|secret\|token\|api_key)\s*[:=]\s*["'][^"']{8,}["']` |

**When reporting:** truncate values to first 4-8 characters. **Never** include full secrets.

## Files That Should NEVER Be Committed

Add to `.gitignore`:
```
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials.*
secrets.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.htpasswd
service-account-key.json
```

## Remediation

1. **Rotate** the exposed credential immediately
2. **Remove** from git history: `git filter-repo` or BFG Repo-Cleaner
3. **Move** to environment variables or secret manager (AWS Secrets Manager, Vault, GCP Secret Manager)
4. **Prevent** with pre-commit hooks: `detect-secrets` or `git-secrets`
5. Enable GitHub **secret scanning** in repository settings

## False Positives

Reduce severity by one level if found in: `**/test/**`, `**/mock/**`, `**/fixtures/**`, `**/example/**`

Ignore placeholder values: `changeme`, `CHANGE_ME`, `REPLACE_ME`, `your-*-here`, `TODO`, `<.*>`, `${.*}`
